A volcano is a mountain that erupts molten rock from the Earth's interior.
Lava flows down its slopes and hardens into fresh rock.
Ash and gas are blasted high into the atmosphere.
The 1991 Mount Pinatubo eruption lowered global temperatures for a year.
Volcanic islands rise when eruptions pile rock above the ocean floor.
Hot springs and geysers are the lingering surface heat of a volcano.

